      "description": "A planning tragedy - Plymouth Viewed from a point on the Hoe the city can be seen as a mish mash of building styles that reflect nothing of the character of the area.  Modern buildings are seen as art forms when seen in isolation and in 'artist's impressions' but, when placed in the overall scene, contribute to a tangled jumble.\nThe tower of St Andrew's church and spire of Charles' church can be made out in this photograph as can the dark top of the Roland Lewinsky building of Plymouth University.",
